WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.073
A company website needs a few sections, a menu, and a way for

00:00:05.073 --> 00:00:06.957
visitors to get in touch.

00:00:06.957 --> 00:00:11.577
In this video, we start from the Agency recipe, edit its sections, add

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:14.130
a contact form, and extend its menu.

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:22.785
The Agency theme comes with a setup recipe of the same name.

00:00:22.785 --> 00:00:28.930
On the Setup screen, open Recipe and choose Agency, described as Ready to use company website.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:32.126
The recipe creates a landing page.

00:00:32.126 --> 00:00:38.240
Its Services, Portfolio, About, Team and Clients sections are Bag parts from the Flows module.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:42.825
A Bag part holds content items inside the landing page, and here each

00:00:42.825 --> 00:00:45.210
one holds items of a single type.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:50.951
Services holds services, each with a title, a description and an icon.

00:00:50.951 --> 00:00:56.467
Portfolio holds projects, About holds milestones, and Team holds team members.

00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:59.160
Clients holds the logos of clients.

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:01.470
We make three changes.

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:05.703
We edit the sections of the landing page, then enable the Forms module

00:01:05.703 --> 00:01:09.490
and build a contact form on its own page, and finally add that

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:11.050
page to the main menu.

00:01:15.235 --> 00:01:18.155
This is the site as the Agency recipe leaves it.

00:01:18.155 --> 00:01:21.725
The landing page opens with the site name and a Tell Me More

00:01:21.725 --> 00:01:25.025
button, and the main menu stays at the top of the page.

00:01:25.496 --> 00:01:30.547
Scrolling down, the Services, Portfolio and About sections follow one another.

00:01:30.547 --> 00:01:34.396
Each section shows the content items held by its Bag part.

00:01:35.936 --> 00:01:41.517
The main menu has entries for Services, Portfolio, About, Team and Contact.

00:01:41.517 --> 00:01:47.236
Selecting Team, and then Contact, scrolls to those sections of the same page.

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:51.704
The headings and the Contact Us section, with its form, come from the

00:01:51.704 --> 00:01:53.578
template of the landing page.

00:01:53.578 --> 00:01:57.539
The items inside the sections are content, and the menu is a content

00:01:57.539 --> 00:02:00.430
item too, so both can be changed from the admin.

00:02:04.693 --> 00:02:07.497
In the admin, open Content, Content Items.

00:02:07.497 --> 00:02:12.112
The list shows the landing page, named after the site, and the Main Menu.

00:02:12.112 --> 00:02:14.273
Click Edit on the landing page.

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:19.840
The editor shows a Title and a Permalink, then one block for each Bag part:

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:23.054
Services, Portfolio, About, Team and Clients.

00:02:23.054 --> 00:02:27.404
The items of a part are cards that you can collapse and expand.

00:02:27.856 --> 00:02:31.450
To change an existing item, edit the fields of its card.

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:35.566
A team member has a Title for the name, an Occupation, a Picture,

00:02:35.566 --> 00:02:37.711
and fields for social profiles.

00:02:37.711 --> 00:02:39.856
We change the first Occupation.

00:02:40.322 --> 00:02:46.232
In Services, the button reads Add Service, because this part holds a single type of item.

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:50.712
Clicking it adds a card, and we enter Brand Identity as its Title.

00:02:51.185 --> 00:02:56.460
Below the Title, the HtmlBody field holds the description, and Icon Class, below

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:58.790
that, names a Font Awesome icon.

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:02.225
We enter a short description and the palette icon.

00:03:02.683 --> 00:03:06.242
Every card has a handle to drag it to another position, and a

00:03:06.242 --> 00:03:07.942
trash button to delete it.

00:03:07.942 --> 00:03:11.183
We drag Brand Identity to the top of the Services part.

00:03:11.661 --> 00:03:12.759
Click Publish.

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:17.316
A message confirms that the Landing Page has been published, and the Services

00:03:17.316 --> 00:03:20.226
section of the site shows Brand Identity first.

00:03:20.226 --> 00:03:23.081
Save Draft would keep the changes unpublished.

00:03:27.346 --> 00:03:32.014
A form is built from widgets, and the Forms module provides them.

00:03:32.014 --> 00:03:36.156
Open Tools, Features, search for Forms, and find its row.

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:37.732
Click Enable.

00:03:37.732 --> 00:03:41.148
A message confirms that the feature Forms was enabled.

00:03:41.148 --> 00:03:45.360
Forms depends on Flows and Widgets, which the Agency recipe enables.

00:03:46.974 --> 00:03:49.362
Let's create the page for the form.

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:53.264
On the Content Items list, open the New menu and choose Page.

00:03:53.716 --> 00:03:55.500
A Page has a Flow part.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:59.744
Like a Bag part, it holds content items inside the page, but by

00:03:59.744 --> 00:04:05.096
default it accepts every widget type, so one page can mix text, images and forms.

00:04:05.715 --> 00:04:10.124
We enter Start a project as the Title, and leave the Permalink empty,

00:04:10.124 --> 00:04:12.476
so it is generated from the Title.

00:04:12.476 --> 00:04:15.886
The plus button titled Add Widget lists the widgets.

00:04:15.886 --> 00:04:16.945
Choose Form.

00:04:20.228 --> 00:04:22.354
A Form widget has its own Title.

00:04:22.354 --> 00:04:27.611
The Action field takes the address that receives the submitted data, such as a workflow.

00:04:27.611 --> 00:04:31.918
We leave it empty here, since handling submissions is a separate topic.

00:04:32.376 --> 00:04:36.857
The Method is POST, and the Anti Forgery Token option is checked, which

00:04:36.857 --> 00:04:39.476
adds an anti forgery token to the form.

00:04:39.965 --> 00:04:44.536
Inside the Form widget, its own plus button adds the form elements.

00:04:44.536 --> 00:04:45.725
Choose Input.

00:04:45.725 --> 00:04:50.170
We enter name as the HTML Name, set the Label option to Standard,

00:04:50.170 --> 00:04:52.925
and enter Your name as the Label Text.

00:04:56.558 --> 00:04:58.948
The Label option has three choices.

00:04:58.948 --> 00:05:03.727
None shows no label, Standard shows the Label Text, and Screen Readers hides

00:05:03.727 --> 00:05:07.458
the label from view but keeps it for assistive technology.

00:05:07.951 --> 00:05:11.029
A second Input collects the email address.

00:05:11.029 --> 00:05:15.326
Its HTML Name is email, its Type is Email, and its Label Text

00:05:15.326 --> 00:05:19.111
is Your email, with the Label option set to Standard.

00:05:19.649 --> 00:05:22.130
A Text Area holds the message.

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:26.953
Its HTML Name is message, and its Label Text is Project details.

00:05:26.953 --> 00:05:31.913
A Button widget closes the form, with the HTML Name send, the Text

00:05:31.913 --> 00:05:34.049
Send and the Type Submit.

00:05:37.098 --> 00:05:38.206
Click Publish.

00:05:38.206 --> 00:05:43.578
A message confirms that the Page has been published, and the list of content items returns.

00:05:47.792 --> 00:05:51.035
Open Content, Menus, and click Edit on Main Menu.

00:05:51.035 --> 00:05:55.458
The editor lists the menu items that the recipe created, and each one

00:05:55.458 --> 00:05:58.112
links to a section of the landing page.

00:05:58.575 --> 00:06:02.156
Add Menu Item opens the Available Menu Items window.

00:06:02.156 --> 00:06:06.662
It offers the Link Menu Item for a custom address, the Content Menu

00:06:06.662 --> 00:06:11.291
Item for a content item, and the Html Menu Item for a link with HTML.

00:06:11.291 --> 00:06:13.575
Let's choose Content Menu Item.

00:06:14.054 --> 00:06:16.608
We enter Start a project as the Name.

00:06:16.608 --> 00:06:21.418
In Selected Content Item, we type to search and select the page we created.

00:06:21.418 --> 00:06:25.574
The menu item links to that page itself, not to a typed address.

00:06:26.025 --> 00:06:31.212
Check content permissions, when selected, verifies that the visitor may view the page

00:06:31.212 --> 00:06:32.979
before the item is shown.

00:06:32.979 --> 00:06:37.767
Its hint warns that this can affect performance, and advises caching the menu,

00:06:37.767 --> 00:06:39.705
which the Agency theme does.

00:06:40.188 --> 00:06:43.282
Click Publish on the menu item to add it to the menu.

00:06:43.282 --> 00:06:46.638
That saves a draft of the menu, so we click Publish on the

00:06:46.638 --> 00:06:49.260
menu as well to show the change to visitors.

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:51.778
Dragging items in this list reorders them.

00:06:56.011 --> 00:07:00.895
On the site, the main menu ends with Start a project, the item we created.

00:07:00.895 --> 00:07:02.971
Selecting it opens the page.

00:07:03.428 --> 00:07:07.082
The page title is the heading, and the form follows it, with a

00:07:07.082 --> 00:07:10.198
label for each field and the Send button at the end.

00:07:14.398 --> 00:07:19.580
The sections you edited are Bag parts, so editing them means editing the items inside.

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:23.127
The contact form is a Form widget on a page, and the menu

00:07:23.127 --> 00:07:24.817
item links to that page.

00:07:24.817 --> 00:07:27.238
Each piece can be changed on its own.

00:07:29.238 --> 00:07:33.941
The Agency recipe gives you a company website whose sections, contact form and

00:07:33.941 --> 00:07:36.013
menu you change from the admin.

00:07:36.013 --> 00:07:37.468
Thanks for watching.

